id: pm-fpdne3
title: Published-artifact verification rejects the new pm-mcp-http bin before executing its healthy published entrypoint
description: "Release v2026.8.26 published successfully to npm, but scripts/release/verify-published-release.mjs hardcodes covered entrypoints to pm and pm-mcp. The declared pm-mcp-http bin is executable in the registry tarball yet is classified as uncovered, blocking installed-agent acceptance and GitHub Release creation. Extend the verifier with a real semantic HTTP-bin assertion and preserve fail-closed coverage for future bins."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[5]: "area:mcp","area:release",published-artifact,regression,release-gate
created_at: "2026-08-26T03:05:50.655Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-26T03:47:54.533Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-26T03:37:39.469Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-26T03:37:39.469Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "The verifier executes pm-mcp-http from the exact public package under both supported executor/install surfaces or an equivalent contained install; It performs a real HTTP server/discover assertion for protocol 2026-07-28; A missing, non-executable, non-listening, or invalid HTTP bin fails; Package-derived coverage remains fail-closed for any future unhandled bin; Focused tests, exact repository coverage, static quality, installed npm/Bun acceptance, and immutable-tag recovery pass"
parent: pm-ygli86
severity: high
resolution: "Extended published-release verification so every declared pm-mcp-http bin is launched from the exact npm package under npx and bunx, probed with a real MCP 2026-07-28 server/discover HTTP exchange, and included in fail-closed package-derived coverage."
expected_result: Every declared package bin has an executable semantic assertion; pm-mcp-http is launched from the exact public package and proves server/discover over HTTP before release advertisement.
actual_result: The repaired verifier accepts the executable public 2026.8.26 pm-mcp-http artifact only after HTTP 200 semantic discovery under both npx and bunx; malformed discovery and future unhandled bins fail in negative controls.
affected_version: 2026.8.26
fixed_version: v2026.8.26 same-tag recovery from reviewed main
component: release verification
regression: true
